<title>JAPAN: CSCE actively reviewing NYMEX building space offer.</title>
<headline>CSCE actively reviewing NYMEX building space offer.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York's Coffee, Sugar &amp; Cocoa Exchange (CSCE) is actively and carefully reviewing the New York Mercantile Exchange's (NYMEX) offer of trading and office space at a new facility, CSCE president James Bowe said during a visit to Tokyo on Tuesday.</p>
<p>He declined to comment further on the offer, however.</p>
<p>NYMEX has offered CSCE and the New York Cotton Exchange 15,000 square feet of trading space and 35,000 square feet of office space at its new building in Manhattan's Battery Park City, due to be occupied from late May.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
